{"title":"1982 USAMO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c7f3f828cf12ab9cafeffad282468a95219600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> is in the interior of an equilateral triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/a/e3a8ae66ded7f33f9385a37c9cadfb82720013d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> is in the interior of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/4/854d714ebe251d0d3fe8dad5dc4a83afda9a299d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{A_1BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"16\" />, prove that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/c/4ccb70a8f23ab31bc83f4d5cb6d43b0cc8cd294d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I.Q. (A_1BC) &gt; I.Q.(A_2BC)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"219\" height=\"18\" />,\n</p><p>where the <i>isoperimetric quotient</i> of a figure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is defined by\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/6/59605bef5fa499b868bb9d25da48807658139b0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I.Q.(F) = \\frac{\\text{Area (F)}}{\\text{[Perimeter (F)]}^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"205\" height=\"44\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, an arbitrary triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> has isoperimetric quotient (using the notation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/3/d33cc80fa8f093e155c5be46d2e5d9da3d7e1ef5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABC]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> for area and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/2/45275f4931a2836f87e929e156f2b66c15dbd580.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = \\frac{a + b + c}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"105\" height=\"37\" />):\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/4/5446232498508437b7a797bd9e7e49d1e0d6eaca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{[ABC]}{4s^2} = \\frac{[ABC]^3}{4s^2 [ABC]^2} = \\frac{r^3 s^3}{4s^2 \\cdot s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)} = \\frac{r^3}{4(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)}\\]\" width=\"598\" height=\"44\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/9/989660aefdfcde9e881ab39eeaacb5798951a179.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\frac{1}{4} \\cdot \\frac{r}{s-a} \\cdot \\frac{r}{s-b} \\cdot \\frac{r}{s-c} = \\frac{1}{4} \\tan A/2 \\tan B/2 \\tan C/2.\\]\" width=\"434\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Lemma. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/1/e01caa3a0c5429b55a02080fb8a371c062c8a200.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan x \\tan (A - x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"128\" height=\"18\" /> is increasing on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c166de640e363daa383883174e4151007b6980c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; x &lt; \\frac{A}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"84\" height=\"38\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/4/90402c1561744489cd23d5dc57b0eb5d27da7ab0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; A &lt; 90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"99\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Proof. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/2/0227a0403c25294417508b570735a601402ba27c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan x \\tan (A - x) = \\tan x \\cdot \\frac{\\tan A - \\tan x}{1 + \\tan A \\tan x} = 1 - \\frac{1}{\\cos^2 x (1 + \\tan A \\tan x)}\\]\" width=\"537\" height=\"42\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/4/5247911c108dc1ab453b8def453fe271d56a61ed.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= 1 - \\frac{2}{1 + \\cos 2x + \\tan A \\sin 2x} = 1 - \\frac{2}{1 + \\sec A \\cos (A - 2x)}\\]\" width=\"470\" height=\"41\" /> is increasing on the desired interval, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/3/5d34bfcf26c9f34b8dba9fbb4dcb4f66f7f839de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos (A - 2x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" /> is increasing on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/2/88237c9a678ba75c437601145bc3e083fd541f51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; x &lt; \\frac{A}{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"89\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/e/d0eebd00c02420b72303b8c5f521965fe6456258.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1, y_1, z_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/2/5c26a12bc32b20413b7e4c192fd664acdb25b51d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2, y_2, z_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"65\" height=\"11\" /> be half of the angles of triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/d/33d4454bb65583c414ab30742fcf80662591c59e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1 BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/8/f5850a0a123f1753ff9ed74716776676ae229deb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_2 BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" /> in that order, respectively. Then it is immediate that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/4/a748f92096a01c8a8fed36bccacb1d2e0c562be1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^\\circ &gt; y_1 &gt; y_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/3481b8081924a1b49029d1bf6f4add3ffac0b8a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^\\circ &gt; z_1 &gt; z_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"104\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/f/2ef4768e8d0d7dc9cd6a87ac5070850108311291.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 + y_1 + z_1 = x_2 + y_2 + z_2 = 90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"261\" height=\"16\" />. Hence, by Lemma it follows that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/d/0fd9cb051af690cb5e8423c1c8f27b1680628105.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan x_1 \\tan y_1 \\tan z_1 = \\tan (90^\\circ - y_1 - z_1) \\tan y_1 \\tan z_1 &gt; \\tan (90^\\circ - y_1 - z_2) \\tan y_1 \\tan z_2\\]\" width=\"638\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/7/a079f11e251c3e377f1ba0542d33856815e9fcf1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[&gt; \\tan (90^\\circ - y_2 - z_2) \\tan y_2 \\tan z_2 = \\tan x_2 \\tan y_2 \\tan z_2.\\]\" width=\"429\" height=\"18\" />\nMultiplying this inequality by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> gives that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/9/d29336270fb31f616ba75fa9409d76d2593d75e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I.Q[A_1 BC] &gt; I.Q[A_2 BC]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"200\" height=\"18\" />, as desired.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_USAMO\" title=\"1982 USAMO\">1982 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1982 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1982\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1982 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1982 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1982 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1982 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1982 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1982 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017173948\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.037 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.063 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 192/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1267/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6073/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.527      1 -total\n 55.40%    6.940      1 Template:USAMO_box\n 42.23%    5.290      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11830:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017173948 and revision id 70309. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}